# Line endings in this tree are load-bearing, and mixed on purpose:
#   app/Progress.ps1          LF only, no BOM
#   app/Transcribe-Entry.ps1  CRLF, with exactly ONE deliberate bare LF (the $claimModel line)
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite both on checkout and
# change every file's SHA-256. That is not cosmetic here: install-manifest.json records the
# SHA-256 of each deployed file and the installer verifies against it, so a checkout that
# "helpfully" normalised line endings would show the whole app as drifted.
#
# -text disables all conversion in both directions. Bytes in, same bytes out.
* -text
